# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This entire file is OPTIONAL. A working key already ships in ".env", so the
# BONUS "nearby live traffic" panel is on straight after `npm install && npm run
# dev` with no setup at all.
#
# Use this file only to override that shared key with your own — recommended if
# you deploy the app, since the committed key is public and shared by everyone
# who clones the repo.
#
# 1. In the Google Cloud Console, create an API key with "Maps JavaScript API"
#    enabled. Optionally also enable "Directions API" — that adds the drive time
#    in current traffic from your location to the selected car park.
# 2. Copy this file to ".env.local":  cp .env.local.example .env.local
# 3. Paste your key below and restart `npm run dev`.
#
# SECURITY: NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are embedded in the browser bundle and are
# visible to everyone. Restrict the key to your own domain with an HTTP referrer
# restriction in the Google Cloud Console. .env.local is in .gitignore.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
